course: dictionary
lesson: 13208
title: The forked bone called furcula
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A furcula is a forked bone. Its name is a Latin word, so you may not know it, but the words around it give clues. «The furcula is the wishbone in a chicken's chest.» A wishbone is a bone shaped like a Y, so furcula must be a forked bone too.
explain: Read on to check. «When the bird flaps its wings, the furcula bends and springs back, a bit like a spring.» Bends and springs back are clues that the furcula is bendy and flexible, not hard and straight. Ask yourself: what would fit in this sentence? A bone that bends and springs back fits well.
explain: The same word can mean different things in different places. «The springtail flicked its furcula and jumped high into the air.» Here a furcula is not a bone at all, but a forked tail-like part of a tiny insect. The clue is the word jumped. Always check the context before you decide what a word means.
fact: A furcula is the wishbone of a bird.
fact: «Furcula» means a forked bone in a bird's chest, made of two collarbones joined together.
fact: In a tiny insect called a springtail, the furcula is a forked part that flicks down to make it jump.
fact: Scientists found furculas in some dinosaurs, which is one clue that birds came from dinosaurs.
fact: The plural of furcula can be furculas or furculae.
exercise: «The furcula is the wishbone in a chicken's chest.» What is a furcula? | A bird's beak | A kind of feather | * The forked bone in a bird's chest | A type of nest
exercise: «The springtail flicked its furcula and jumped high into the air.» What does the furcula do here? | It helps the springtail swim | It keeps the springtail warm | It lays eggs | * It flicks down to make the springtail jump
exercise: Ben and Mia each pulled one end of the chicken's furcula and made a wish. What word in this sentence is another name for the furcula? | Dinner | Pulled | * Wishbone | Chicken
test: «Scientists found furculas in some dinosaurs.» What does this sentence tell you about birds and dinosaurs? | * Birds may have come from dinosaurs | Dinosaurs could fly like birds today | Birds and dinosaurs have no bones at all | Dinosaurs were all very small
test: «When the bird flaps its wings, the furcula springs back like a spring.» What does the furcula work like? | A stone | * A spring | A wing | A feather
exam: «The furcula bends, then springs back when the wings flap.» What is the best meaning of furcula? | A soft fluffy feather | A forked bone in a bird's chest, or a forked part that makes a springtail jump | * A forked bone in a bird's chest, or a forked part that makes a springtail jump | A type of rock found under the sea
